<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The Aspire AppHost for the example: it declares the Postgres server, the database on it, the Quartz.NET
    dashboard and the worker that uses them, and nothing else. It is in the solution so that `Compile` fails
    when the documented AppHost wiring stops compiling — which is the whole reason it exists, since an
    AppHost builds without a container runtime.

    Aspire 17's shape: Microsoft.NET.Sdk and two packages, Aspire.Hosting.AppHost for the AppHost's build
    targets and Aspire.Hosting.Dotnet for AddDotnetProject. Aspire.AppHost.Sdk is obsolete from 17 (ASPIRE012)
    and AddProject<T> with it (CS0618), and both are errors here. Every Aspire package is at $(AspireVersion);
    Quartz.Aspire.Hosting, referenced below, is built against its own floor, Aspire.Hosting 13.6.5, and this
    project resolves that to the 17 the packages ask for. This is the one place the two meet at run time.

    The worker is not a ProjectReference: AddDotnetProject takes its path, and Aspire builds it before it
    starts it. No ProjectReference is a project resource either, unless it says IsAspireProjectResource="true".

    A C# AppHost needs the Aspire CLI bundle, the dashboard and the Developer Control Plane, from 17 on
    (ASPIRE013, which cannot be suppressed). Restore no longer brings them as packages. Building does: it
    looks for the bundle in the Aspire home, ~/.aspire or ASPIRE_HOME, and when none is there it runs
    `aspire setup`, with the `aspire` on PATH or, without one, `dnx aspire.cli@$(AspireVersion)`. So a machine
    with neither the CLI nor a bundle, a CI runner, downloads the CLI (about 180 MB) the first time it builds
    this project, and has to reach nuget.org to do it. A bundle that is already there is used whatever its
    version; `dotnet run` hands the AppHost to the CLI's `aspire run`, which brings its own.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <SignAssembly>false</SignAssembly>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Aspire.Hosting.AppHost" />
    <PackageReference Include="Aspire.Hosting.Dotnet" />
    <PackageReference Include="Aspire.Hosting.PostgreSQL" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenTelemetry.Exporter.OpenTelemetryProtocol" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The dashboard resource, AddQuartzDashboard and WithReference(dashboard). -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Quartz.Aspire.Hosting\Quartz.Aspire.Hosting.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
